2. Show me the rolling 3-month average revenue and flag any month where revenue dropped more than 15% compared to the same month last year

1.  What is the total revenue for all time?
    → resolves: Revenue → SUM(total_sales)

2.  How many orders were placed in 2023?
    → resolves: Orders → COUNT(order_id), Date → sales_date

3.  What is the total number of units sold by each car make?
    → resolves: Units Sold → SUM(order_qty), Car → make
Synonym Resolution (Where Semantic Layer Proves Its Value)
4.  Who are the top 10 sellers by turnover?
    → resolves: sellers   → Salesperson (dim_salesman)
                turnover  → Revenue → SUM(total_sales)

5.  Show me total earnings by automobile brand
    → resolves: earnings  → Revenue → SUM(total_sales)
                automobile → Vehicle → dim_carline
                brand      → make (attribute of dim_carline)

6.  Which agents generated the most income last year?
    → resolves: agents    → Salesperson
                income    → Revenue → SUM(total_sales)

7.  What is the basket size per transaction by vehicle type?
    → resolves: basket size      → Revenue Per Order
                                   SUM(total_sales)/NULLIF(COUNT(order_id),0)
                transaction      → Orders
                vehicle type     → car_type (attribute of dim_carline)
Multi-Dimension Complex Joins
8.  Show monthly revenue breakdown by car type and paint colour
    → resolves: monthly        → Date hierarchy → strftime('%Y-%m', sales_date)
                revenue        → SUM(total_sales)
                car type       → dim_carline.car_type
                paint colour   → dim_color.colour_name
    → requires: fact_sales
                JOIN dim_carline ON carline_id
                JOIN dim_color   ON colour_id
                GROUP BY month, car_type, colour_name

9.  Which salesperson sold the most vehicles in Q3 2023
    and what was their average selling price?
    → resolves: salesperson    → first_name || ' ' || last_name
                vehicles       → Units Sold → SUM(order_qty)
                Q3 2023        → Date → BETWEEN '2023-07-01' AND '2023-09-30'
                avg price      → Average Selling Price
                               → SUM(total_sales)/NULLIF(SUM(order_qty),0)
    → requires: fact_sales JOIN dim_salesman ON sales_person_id

10. Compare revenue per rep across all active salespeople
    by engine type for the Ford make
    → resolves: revenue per rep  → Revenue Per Salesperson
                active           → dim_salesman.active = TRUE
                engine type      → dim_carline.engine_type
                Ford             → dim_carline.make = 'Ford'
    → requires: fact_sales
                JOIN dim_salesman ON sales_person_id
                JOIN dim_carline  ON carline_id
Hierarchy + Drill-Down Questions
11. Show the vehicle drill from make down to car line
    for the top 5 revenue-generating models
    → resolves via Vehicle_Hierarchy:
                make → car_type → model → carline_name
                revenue → SUM(total_sales)

12. Show year over year revenue trend
    → resolves via Date_Hierarchy:
                Year → strftime('%Y', sales_date)
                revenue → SUM(total_sales)
    → GPT generates:
                SELECT strftime('%Y', sales_date) AS year,
                       SUM(total_sales) AS revenue
                FROM   fact_sales
                GROUP BY year
                ORDER BY year

13. What is the quarterly sales volume by colour for 2022 and 2023?
    → resolves: quarterly   → strftime('%Y-Q', sales_date)
                sales volume → Units Sold → SUM(order_qty)
                colour       → dim_color.colour_name
    → requires: fact_sales JOIN dim_color ON colour_id
Productivity & Ratio Measures
14. What is the productivity of each sales consultant
    broken down by car brand?
    → resolves: productivity   → Revenue Per Salesperson
                               → SUM(total_sales)/NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT
                                 sales_person_id),0)
                consultant     → Salesperson
                car brand      → dim_carline.make

15. Show headcount and revenue per agent
    for each engine type ranked highest to lowest
    → resolves: headcount      → Active Salespeople
                               → COUNT(DISTINCT sales_person_id)
                revenue per    → Revenue Per Salesperson
                agent
                engine type    → dim_carline.engine_type